CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* bool from a call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* class from a call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* function declaration: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
N5008 [dcl.ambig.res]/1: `bool b(rd());' declares a function only if rd names
a type.  For a function rd, the declaration was turned into a variable whose
initializer was the function itself, so `b' was `(bool)&rd' and rd was never
called; a class type rejected the initializer.
